    "fullSolution": "$7^{100} \\pmod{13}$\n\nSince $13$ is prime and $\\gcd(7,13) = 1$, by Fermat's Little Theorem:\n$$7^{12} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{13}$$\n\nWrite $100 = 12 \\times 8 + 4$:\n$$7^{100} = 7^{96+4} = (7^{12})^8 \\cdot 7^4 \\equiv 1^8 \\cdot 7^4 \\equiv 7^4 \\pmod{13}$$\n\nCompute $7^4$:\n$$7^2 = 49 \\equiv 10 \\pmod{13}$$\n$$7^4 = (7^2)^2 \\equiv 10^2 = 100 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{13}$$\n\nTherefore: $7^{100} \\equiv 9 \\pmod{13}$",
